WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.360
Bill Skarsgård has been working as an actor
since 2000, with some of his earliest roles

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.900
including a small role in a film called "White
Water Fury" in 2000 and a two-episode arc

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.840
on a miniseries called "Laura Trenter — Dad,
the Policeman" in 2002, both of which are

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:21.600
Swedish projects. A decade later, he began
his run as a main cast member on the horror

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.140
series "Hemlock Grove," which went on to have
three total seasons. However, it was his role

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:32.829
as Pennywise the Clown in the 2017 film adaptation
of Stephen King's "It" that really brought

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:35.250
public attention to the Swedish actor.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.890
Since then, Skarsgård has starred in Season
1 of the horror anthology series "Castle Rock"

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:46.309
in 2018, reprised his role as Pennywise for
"It Chapter Two" in 2019, and acted in a string

00:00:46.309 --> 00:00:53.309
of films, including "Nine Days" and "The Devil
All the Time," both of which came out in 2020.

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:59.359
He also voiced the character of Kro for Marvel's
"Eternals," which came out in late 2021. The

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:04.460
actor also has quite a few upcoming projects,
including "John Wick: Chapter 4" and a TV

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:09.610
drama called "Clark," in which the youngest
Skarsgård brother plays the titular character,

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.560
a charming yet infamous Swedish gangster.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.020
Clearly, Skarsgård has a lot on his plate,
but, were he to find the time to play the

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.450
part, there is one iconic character that one
pop culture fan has in mind for him, and it's

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.450
the Joker.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:28.020
Artist William Gray, who describes himself
on Instagram as a, quote, "creator of pop

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.540
culture-inspired Photoshop pieces," has made
Bill Skarsgård a frequent figure in his reimaginings

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:39.119
of popular character actors depicted as Gotham's
notorious Clown Prince of Crime. In recent

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:44.110
months, Skarsgård has appeared nearly a dozen
times on the artist's grid, shown in various

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:48.750
costumes and make-up looks in each stunning
rendering. The end results are proof that

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:52.869
the actor could make a terrifying version
of the villainous character. One of the more

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:57.770
recent pictures depicts a Skarsgård's Joker
being carted, Hannibal Lecter-style, into

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:58.890
Arkham Asylum. An image from October 2020,
and another from September 2020, show close-up

00:01:58.890 --> 00:01:59.890
versions of the Joker.

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.920
One look at the comments of the photos, and
it is crystal clear that movie fans are on

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.290
board for Skarsgård as the Joker. With the
first photo, one user wrote,

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.220
"Holy s— that actually looks perfect ... in
my opinion."

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.270
Another user chimed in, complete with the
fire emoji,

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:19.220
"Will, you are a genius Bill Skarsgård would
be a perfect Joker."

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.470
With the third photo, yet another Instagram
user commented,

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:25.910
"I so want Skarsgård to be the next Joker."

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:30.660
Elsewhere in the comment thread, one user
simply wrote, "Creepy" with three clown emojis

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.660
tacked on.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.200
Overall, it's safe to say that Gray has convinced
us that Skarsgård would fit right into the

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:41.700
role. Sure, he's not the only actor the artist
has reimagined as Joker (Johnny Depp, Crispin

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:46.760
Glover, and Jim Carrey also get the transformation
treatment), but Gray's vision of Skargård

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:51.810
as the bone-chilling criminal is arguably
one of the most convincing.

